      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "`kg:processes` and `kg:files` — an instance's diagrams and files, from its declaration",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-09-29: *\"display bpmn(s) etc in README.md\"*, *\"part of readme.md generation is to do rendering\"*, and the file list at the end must be *\"a skill and tool in cat-harness\"*.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "Owner",
        "2026-09-29"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-29"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/readme-sections.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "`kg:processes` and `kg:files` — an instance's diagrams and files, from its declaration",
      "prov:value": "This section **reads** the SVG and never draws; rendering needs a browser, so `render:bpmn` must run first. bootstrap's own README is generated and checked in bootstrap's repository (owner, 2026-10-01: each repo owns its README; litlfred/bootstrap#1).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "owner",
        "bootstrap#1",
        "2026-10-01"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/readme-sections.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "`subgraph-readmes` — one README per declared directory",
      "prov:value": "**The layout is Liquid**, in `bootstrap-tools/scripts/templates/readme/`, beside the writer in the tools repository (bean `xsqm`). cat-harness's `readme:subgraphs` resolves its own Extensions — a directory's `scope`, an `absent` directory, the declared README — and calls that writer.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean `xsqm`"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/readme-sections.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "`subgraph-readmes` — one README per declared directory",
      "prov:value": "`--check` fails on a stale README — the READMEs are docs, committed — and **judges** the record rather than comparing it: it fails on a declared directory newly absent or a process newly unresolved against a baseline, and a missing baseline is UNKNOWN and not gated (bean `0dav`). The record itself is a derived QA result whose home is the `qa-reports` branch (arc `3fva`), so it is not something to regenerate and commit.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean `0dav`",
        "arc `3fva`"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/readme-sections.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Maintaining these files is memory work, not documentation work",
      "prov:value": "Keeping them true is part of [`agent-memory`](../../conduct/conduct-core/agent-memory.md), and the owner put them there:",
